---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaCatchDoms from '../../components/CtaCatchDoms.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config.js';

const breadcrumb = [
  { name: 'Expired Domains', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' },
  { name: 'How to buy expired domains', href: '/guides/how-to-buy-expired-domains/' },
];

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'How to buy expired domains',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name },
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to Buy Expired Domains — 3 Practical Methods"
  description="Learn how to buy expired domains: register fresh drops, bid at auctions, or place a backorder. A practical guide with the checks to run first."
  breadcrumb={breadcrumb}
  schema={schema}
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How to buy expired domains</h1>
    <p>
      There are three practical ways to acquire an <a href="/">expired domain</a>, depending on where it is
      in its lifecycle. Here is how each works and when to use it.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Register a fresh drop</h2>
    <p>
      Once a domain fully drops, anyone can register it at a standard registrar for the regular price.
      The catch: good names get caught fast. Monitoring tools surface them the moment they become available.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Bid at auction</h2>
    <p>
      Many expiring domains are sold through auctions before they ever drop. You bid against others, and the
      highest bid wins. This is common for names with traffic or strong authority.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Place a backorder</h2>
    <p>
      A backorder is an order to attempt registration the instant a specific domain drops. Useful when you
      have a target name and want to automate the catch.
    </p>

    <h2>Checks to run before you buy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/tools/whois-lookup/">WHOIS lookup</a> — confirm registrar, dates and status.</li>
      <li><a href="/tools/domain-age-checker/">Domain age</a> — older usually means more accrued authority.</li>
      <li><a href="/tools/dns-lookup/">DNS lookup</a> — see whether it is still configured.</li>
      <li>Backlink quality and topical relevance — the real drivers of value.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Want the theory first? Read <a href="/guides/what-is-an-expired-domain/">what is an expired domain</a>,
      or jump to <a href="/guides/expired-domains-for-seo/">expired domains for SEO</a>.
    </p>
  </article>

  <CtaCatchDoms text="CatchDoms aggregates expired and auction domains from 11 registrars in one place." label="Find domains to buy" />
</BaseLayout>
